   "evidence": "The exact precedent is `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Weights/TensorProduct.lean`, which holds the weight spaces of a tensor product as a standalone file (imports `Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.TensorProduct`, `Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Weights.Basic` only) and leaves the character to its consumer; `Weights/Prod.lean` does not yet exist (glob of `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Weights/**`). The `omit [LinearWeights ...] [FiniteDimensional ...]` lines at 206, 222, 245, 252, 266, 279 are themselves the evidence that these results need none of the file's ambient hypotheses.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Weights/FormalCharacter.lean",
   "fix": "Move those six declarations to a new `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Weights/Prod.lean` importing `Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.Weights.Linear` and `TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Prod`, and import it from `FormalCharacter.lean`; keep only `formalCharacter_prod` here.",
   "issue": "The whole `Prod` block except `formalCharacter_prod` \u2014 `mem_genWeightSpace_prod_iff` (212), `genWeightSpace_prod_eq_bot_iff` (226), `genWeightSpace_ne_bot_or` (248), `instLinearWeightsProd` (255), `genWeightSpaceProdEquiv` (269), `finrank_genWeightSpace_prod` (281) \u2014 is general weight theory of `M \u00d7 N` with no reference to the character. It uses only `LieModule.genWeightSpace`/`LinearWeights` and `TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Prod`, i.e. nothing from `Integrality`, `WeylInvariance`, `Dimension.DirectSum` or `MonoidAlgebra`. Placing it here means any later file wanting the `LinearWeights K L (M \u00d7 N)` instance or the simp lemma must import the Killing-semisimple weight theory and the integral group algebra.",
   "line": 206
  }
